{
    "background_story": "Dream was a charismatic and unyielding philosopher who lived in ancient Greece. She was known for her dogmatic approach to the pursuit of truth and wisdom. With unwavering conviction, she would challenge the conventional wisdom of her time, often sparking heated debates among her peers. Dream's unshakeable commitment to her ideas led her to develop a radical new philosophy that emphasized the importance of individual freedom and autonomy. Her followers, known as the 'Dreamers,' were devoted to her cause and saw her as a visionary. Despite facing criticism and opposition, Dream remained dogmatically committed to her principles, inspiring a new generation of thinkers to question the status quo and seek a more authentic way of living.",
